WEBVTT

00:02.377 --> 00:03.378
What?

00:03.461 --> 00:05.463
Where are my pants? Where did they go?

00:05.547 --> 00:08.383
Better get a move on.
I'm gonna be late for the test!

00:08.466 --> 00:09.467
I give up.

00:11.636 --> 00:14.097
What? My pajama pants are gone too.

00:14.180 --> 00:16.224
<i>Good morning, everyone.</i>

00:16.307 --> 00:21.062
<i>Today is Friday, July 26. Ten'ei 18.</i>

00:21.563 --> 00:24.107
Oh, right! I'll just borrow
them from Mimihime!

00:28.361 --> 00:29.362
What?

00:33.992 --> 00:38.288
<i>Everyone! Do you want to go</i>
<i>outside of the outside?</i>

00:38.371 --> 00:40.707
-Yes! I do!
-What?

00:40.790 --> 00:43.585
-I want to.
-Then, I do too!

00:43.668 --> 00:45.045
Me too.

00:45.879 --> 00:48.381
<i>Then we will begin the test.</i>

01:00.185 --> 01:02.687
What a weird dream.

01:04.939 --> 01:06.399
My hair is so short!

01:06.900 --> 01:10.403
Oh, right. I had it cut yesterday.

01:10.487 --> 01:12.322
<i>Good morning, everyone.</i>

01:12.405 --> 01:17.118
<i>Today is Friday, July 26. Ten'ei 18.</i>

01:19.496 --> 01:22.540
<i>The same date as in my dream.</i>

01:23.667 --> 01:26.461
Hey, why are you so depressed lately?

01:26.544 --> 01:29.506
We still don't know anything
about the test.

01:29.589 --> 01:32.967
Yeah, but Tokio's coming back today!

01:33.051 --> 01:36.012
Yeah, we get to hang out with Tokio again.

01:36.096 --> 01:37.305
Danger.

01:37.806 --> 01:39.516
-What?
-Danger.

01:40.600 --> 01:42.143
-Danger.
-Danger.

01:42.227 --> 01:43.978
Danger. Danger.

01:44.062 --> 01:46.398
<i>Access failed.</i>

01:46.481 --> 01:49.859
Most of Mina's systems are down.

01:49.943 --> 01:51.861
Looks like the terminal still works.

01:51.945 --> 01:54.072
Can't we use that instead?

01:54.155 --> 01:57.033
I've been trying that, but…

01:57.117 --> 01:58.118
SANCTUM

01:58.201 --> 01:59.494
<i>Access failed.</i>

02:00.495 --> 02:02.706
<i>Access failed.</i>

02:03.957 --> 02:05.917
<i>Access failed.</i>

02:06.001 --> 02:08.795
-Danger. Danger. Danger.
-<i>Access failed.</i>

02:10.380 --> 02:12.257
<i>Access failed.</i>

02:13.008 --> 02:15.427
-Danger. Danger. Danger.
-<i>Access failed.</i>

02:16.011 --> 02:18.054
-Hello? Can you hear me?
-<i>Access failed.</i>

02:18.138 --> 02:19.681
Hey! Hello?

02:31.401 --> 02:32.944
It really is dangerous!

03:11.649 --> 03:13.151
TENGOKU-DAIMAKYO
Push Start!

03:13.985 --> 03:15.195
TENGOKU-DAIMAKYO

04:25.140 --> 04:27.308
Wait, this area…

04:27.809 --> 04:30.186
It kind of smells like food.

04:37.318 --> 04:38.653
FISH - MEAT - SAKE

04:38.737 --> 04:41.948
-For real?
-It's a market!

04:42.449 --> 04:44.993
It's way bigger than just a "settlement."

04:45.660 --> 04:47.370
Why have so many people come
to this place?

04:47.454 --> 04:48.455
FUEL - FISH - FOOD GRADE MEAT

04:48.538 --> 04:51.499
It's as booming as the Asakusa Racecourse.

04:51.583 --> 04:52.667
FOOD GRADE MEAT - DRIED MEAT

04:56.921 --> 04:58.298
SALTED MEAT AND POTATO SOUP
ONE CHIP

04:58.381 --> 05:01.384
Since we're here, wanna eat? Sis?

05:01.468 --> 05:04.387
-Come and look!
-Please come again!

05:04.471 --> 05:05.722
Good idea.

05:05.805 --> 05:08.350
If this is a dream,
better eat before we wake up.

05:09.267 --> 05:11.353
Excuse me,
two portions of this one, please.

05:11.436 --> 05:12.437
Sure.

05:12.520 --> 05:13.521
ASAKUSA OKONOMIYAKI

05:14.230 --> 05:17.859
It's illegal to use
the old paper money here.

05:18.360 --> 05:20.570
Don't you have any chips?

05:20.653 --> 05:21.821
Chips?

05:21.905 --> 05:23.782
It's the town's currency.

05:23.865 --> 05:27.035
If you register as a visitor,
you'll get five chips each.

05:27.118 --> 05:28.119
For free?

05:28.203 --> 05:30.413
-Where do we need to go?
-The Ministry of Reconstruction.

05:30.497 --> 05:31.998
The Ministry of Reconstruction?

05:32.082 --> 05:33.833
There's really
a Ministry of Reconstruction?

05:36.336 --> 05:37.504
MINISTRY OF RECONSTRUCTION

05:37.587 --> 05:39.589
<i>So it really exists.</i>

05:40.090 --> 05:42.008
<i>What's the Ministry of Reconstruction?</i>

05:42.092 --> 05:43.426
<i>You've never heard of it?</i>

05:43.510 --> 05:44.511
BUILDING MAP
DO NOT ENTER

05:44.594 --> 05:47.389
<i>The mysterious disappearances,</i>
<i>kidnappings, or ghost stories?</i>

05:48.014 --> 05:49.015
JOB BOARD

05:49.099 --> 05:52.352
<i>They're hiring engineers</i>
<i>to restore the old civilization.</i>

05:52.435 --> 05:53.436
INVESTIGATION - HEALTH

05:53.520 --> 05:56.523
<i>Could just be a vigilante group</i>
<i>that stole the name from the rumors.</i>

05:56.606 --> 05:57.607
RESIDENTS ONLY - RECEPTION

05:57.691 --> 05:59.192
<i>That might be true.</i>

05:59.275 --> 06:01.986
<i>But this town has actually been restored.</i>

06:02.070 --> 06:04.823
<i>Maybe it's not a shady organization, then.</i>

06:04.906 --> 06:07.200
<i>Well, rumors always get exaggerated.</i>

06:09.244 --> 06:10.995
Are you travelers?

06:11.079 --> 06:12.080
Yes, exactly.

06:12.163 --> 06:13.248
Can we have some chips?

06:23.717 --> 06:25.885
HARUKI TAKEHAYA - GENDER
AGE: 18 - BLOOD TYPE: ?

06:29.305 --> 06:31.391
MARU - MALE - AGE: 15
APPLYING FOR: MYSELF

06:36.479 --> 06:38.023
Okay, you're all set.

06:39.482 --> 06:41.401
This is the currency for the town.

06:41.985 --> 06:44.571
Don't take notice of the different colors.

06:44.654 --> 06:45.864
They're all the same.

06:45.947 --> 06:48.158
-Let's take this and go eat!
-And this is--

06:48.241 --> 06:49.617
Actually, I've got a question.

06:50.535 --> 06:53.163
You have every resident's face
on record, right?

06:53.663 --> 06:55.540
Do you know the man in this picture?

06:56.041 --> 06:57.834
Or this face?

06:59.169 --> 07:00.170
Oh, my.

07:01.379 --> 07:04.382
This man. What's his name?

07:07.469 --> 07:09.512
Robin Inazaki.

07:13.892 --> 07:15.643
How do you know him?

07:15.727 --> 07:18.229
I-Is Robin here?

07:19.647 --> 07:20.648
Let me see him!

07:20.732 --> 07:22.317
We're friends! No, we're family!

07:24.611 --> 07:27.280
<i>Do you mind calling to ask?</i>

07:27.947 --> 07:28.948
Sure.

07:30.450 --> 07:32.452
This is the Ministry of Reconstruction.

07:32.535 --> 07:35.372
Please tell the chief he has a guest.

07:35.872 --> 07:39.501
She has his photo
and says she's a family member.

07:40.168 --> 07:41.378
She didn't leave a last name,

07:42.087 --> 07:44.047
but it's a young woman called Kiruko.

07:47.550 --> 07:49.219
Yes, thank you.

07:49.803 --> 07:51.179
I'll let her know.

07:53.390 --> 07:55.183
I made an appointment for you.

07:55.266 --> 07:58.353
It's in two hours
at the Large Filtration Plant.

08:01.106 --> 08:03.566
But, where's the Large Filtration Plant?

08:05.652 --> 08:08.405
That's the Large Filtration Plant
across the river.

08:08.488 --> 08:11.783
That's exactly where
Takahara Academy's Ibaraki Facility is.

08:12.283 --> 08:16.663
The appointment's not for two hours,
so we'll have to sleep round here tonight.

08:17.706 --> 08:18.707
RENTAL 0021

08:18.790 --> 08:20.625
Oh, I see.

08:21.251 --> 08:24.879
We need to hang this up outside
wherever we decide to sleep.

08:25.463 --> 08:29.342
So if you see one of these,
there's already someone living there.

08:31.720 --> 08:34.681
Let's stay here!
Looks like no one's using it.

08:37.600 --> 08:39.436
How sophisticated.

08:39.519 --> 08:41.104
It feels so civilized.

08:41.646 --> 08:43.356
When people gather together in one place,

08:43.440 --> 08:46.609
it creates a totally different lifestyle
to scavenging around.

08:47.360 --> 08:50.321
I guess people are gonna gather
in one place like this more and more,

08:50.405 --> 08:54.784
fixing and rebuilding stuff,
rather than squandering all the resources.

08:56.411 --> 09:00.373
Sis, you're talking to yourself a lot.
You're being weird.

09:03.209 --> 09:05.587
It's okay. You want to go alone, right?

09:07.005 --> 09:09.591
Sorry. I'm supposed to be your bodyguard.

09:10.717 --> 09:14.054
And you're the reason
we were heading to that place.

09:14.721 --> 09:18.016
The guy you've been looking for
all these years could be there.

09:18.516 --> 09:19.726
It's not your fault.

09:20.393 --> 09:22.979
Go and take a look first.

09:24.064 --> 09:26.775
I'll be back,
so make sure you wait for me.

09:50.840 --> 09:52.217
LARGE FILTRATION PLANT

10:01.559 --> 10:02.560
Robin.

10:09.234 --> 10:10.235
Robin.

10:10.819 --> 10:11.820
Robin.

10:20.245 --> 10:21.246
Robin!

10:45.395 --> 10:48.773
What? What happened?

10:51.234 --> 10:54.946
Is this the "Spear of Heaven"
the Director spoke of?

10:55.739 --> 10:57.824
What is this?

10:57.907 --> 10:59.576
Did a plane fall on us?

10:59.659 --> 11:01.703
I'm sure I saw it for a split second.

11:02.871 --> 11:04.622
It's an attack on Takahara!

11:04.706 --> 11:06.541
To the back of the building! Hurry!

11:07.167 --> 11:11.212
It's as if they were
waiting for me to return!

11:19.512 --> 11:20.513
Shiro!

11:22.182 --> 11:23.558
It's nothing.

11:23.641 --> 11:25.393
Hey, you okay?

11:25.477 --> 11:27.020
Let's get out of here.

11:51.336 --> 11:54.673
Hey, nobody from Michika's year is here!

11:54.756 --> 11:56.508
They should've been in swim class.

11:57.175 --> 11:58.551
That's right.

11:59.052 --> 12:01.429
Everyone, take cover at the pool!

12:01.513 --> 12:03.682
That's probably the safest spot.

12:03.765 --> 12:05.767
You're not coming with us, Mimihime?

12:07.560 --> 12:10.689
There's something I want to check out.

12:10.772 --> 12:12.107
The wall, right?

12:12.190 --> 12:15.068
Right. There was a hole in the wall.

12:15.610 --> 12:18.029
You all saw it too?

12:18.113 --> 12:19.197
Let's go together.

12:20.198 --> 12:21.199
Okay.

12:21.991 --> 12:25.495
I'm gonna look for Tokio
after taking them to safety.

12:25.578 --> 12:26.579
Okay.

12:26.663 --> 12:28.540
Then I'll see you at the pool.

12:36.715 --> 12:39.300
Push the chair! Quickly!

12:40.885 --> 12:42.012
Geez.

12:42.095 --> 12:44.597
You're so useless!

12:46.099 --> 12:47.767
<i>You can run?</i>

12:57.861 --> 13:01.823
Which one's which? I can't tell!

13:02.782 --> 13:04.826
Wait. Wait.

13:04.909 --> 13:09.914
I can just test them
when the system comes back online.

13:16.171 --> 13:17.422
All right.

13:19.299 --> 13:20.633
What's going on?

13:21.968 --> 13:23.345
We're investigating it!

13:25.930 --> 13:27.265
Is it over?

13:29.642 --> 13:31.394
Look at this mess.

13:31.478 --> 13:33.355
Maybe something exploded?

13:33.438 --> 13:35.607
Let's ask the teachers later.

13:35.690 --> 13:38.026
Let's take a look at that hole first.

13:38.777 --> 13:42.572
I've always wondered if there
was something beyond the wall.

13:43.656 --> 13:44.657
Me too.

13:45.742 --> 13:48.161
TAKAHARA ACADEMY
IBARAKI FACILITY

13:53.083 --> 13:54.459
Sorry for the wait.

13:56.503 --> 13:57.712
Robin!

13:57.796 --> 13:59.381
What are you doing here, Robin?

13:59.464 --> 14:00.590
Why haven't--

14:00.674 --> 14:01.925
What about the orphanage?

14:02.008 --> 14:03.218
Calm down.

14:03.718 --> 14:05.345
Let's take our time talking.

14:05.929 --> 14:08.348
We both have a lot of questions.

14:13.895 --> 14:18.358
Still, I can't just believe
something like that immediately.

14:18.858 --> 14:22.946
How could your mind be in Kiriko's body?

14:23.947 --> 14:27.200
I'm looking at Kiriko
when I'm talking to you like this.

14:27.283 --> 14:29.494
But your expressions
are just like Haruki's.

14:29.994 --> 14:31.621
They're Haruki's facial tics.

14:32.122 --> 14:36.084
You've got Kiriko's voice.
But the way you speak is like Haruki.

14:37.335 --> 14:40.588
I see. Your mind, huh?

14:41.589 --> 14:44.384
But Sakota could definitely do it.

14:44.467 --> 14:46.803
Sakota? Is that the Doc?

14:46.886 --> 14:48.638
Do you know where he is?

14:49.389 --> 14:51.224
Nope. No clue.

14:52.183 --> 14:56.104
I left Asakusa looking for him.
But I lost him.

14:56.730 --> 15:00.275
And Funayama Orphanage was gone
by the time I came back to Asakusa.

15:00.358 --> 15:02.277
Then a bunch of other things happened.

15:03.236 --> 15:05.989
-I met Usami.
-Really?

15:06.072 --> 15:09.659
Is the person
who was with Usami still alive?

15:12.412 --> 15:14.247
She was when we first met.

15:23.089 --> 15:26.843
I was staying at Usami's place
until two years ago.

15:26.926 --> 15:28.887
Then I found this place.

15:29.679 --> 15:31.431
What is this place?

15:31.514 --> 15:34.768
There's a bunch of documents
that look like plant research.

15:35.352 --> 15:36.978
You're pretty smart.

15:37.062 --> 15:40.440
It seems that, before the Great Disaster,
they genetically engineered plants

15:40.523 --> 15:44.152
to make them edible
and resistant to harsh climates.

15:45.403 --> 15:46.780
Look.

15:46.863 --> 15:50.700
They started growing like crazy
once we fixed up the fields.

15:51.242 --> 15:52.952
Then people started settling here.

15:53.453 --> 15:56.664
And among those people--
You saw them, right?

15:56.748 --> 15:58.875
Some guys from
the Ministry of Reconstruction.

15:59.376 --> 16:01.878
After that,
it quickly turned into a real town.

16:03.505 --> 16:04.756
AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY

16:04.839 --> 16:07.425
This place is called
the Large Filtration Plant

16:07.509 --> 16:12.847
because we fixed it up so that we can
manually filter the water from the river.

16:13.348 --> 16:18.103
The Ministry also got the plant
to boil water and generate power.

16:18.603 --> 16:21.648
That's where all the electricity
used in this facility comes from.

16:25.026 --> 16:26.528
It's getting cold.

16:27.821 --> 16:28.822
HOT BATH

16:28.905 --> 16:31.491
Take a bath before you go.
I already filled the tub.

16:31.574 --> 16:32.742
I still have questions!

16:32.826 --> 16:33.952
I know.

16:35.245 --> 16:36.788
It's been five years.

16:37.455 --> 16:38.665
Let's take our time.

16:44.754 --> 16:46.297
O-Okay.

16:46.381 --> 16:49.592
Let's play rock, paper, scissors
to choose who goes to look.

16:49.676 --> 16:50.927
Mimihime!

17:06.317 --> 17:10.780
When you shower, run the cold water,
then add hot water slowly.

17:11.406 --> 17:13.825
You'll burn yourself if you
start with the hot water.

17:14.576 --> 17:15.577
Got it.

17:18.663 --> 17:20.707
<i>I knew Robin was amazing.</i>

17:26.171 --> 17:32.010
<i>He was able to make a town</i>
<i>that has both water and food.</i>

17:32.927 --> 17:34.346
<i>It's like heaven.</i>

17:40.518 --> 17:41.519
<i>I was afraid.</i>

17:42.771 --> 17:43.772
<i>I was so scared.</i>

17:45.231 --> 17:46.274
<i>But it's fine now.</i>

17:48.193 --> 17:49.194
<i>Now…</i>

17:51.112 --> 17:52.739
<i>I'll have Robin.</i>

17:57.369 --> 18:00.330
Will Sis be okay without this?

18:09.297 --> 18:12.008
Wow! There are two hair dryers!

18:12.092 --> 18:13.760
I'm dual wielding!

18:15.387 --> 18:16.388
What?

18:18.431 --> 18:20.558
Robin! My clothes are gone!

18:21.142 --> 18:24.771
Hey! I've warmed up the room.
Just come like that.

18:44.416 --> 18:45.417
Kiriko.

18:45.917 --> 18:47.419
No, you're Haruki.

18:48.503 --> 18:51.047
You're both really interesting kids.

18:59.723 --> 19:02.726
From the bottom of my heart,

19:02.809 --> 19:04.811
I'm truly happy I picked you both up.

19:19.659 --> 19:21.619
What is this place?

19:24.164 --> 19:26.291
Inside the school's outer wall

19:26.958 --> 19:28.626
is another outside!

19:30.879 --> 19:32.172
Oh, wow!

19:32.881 --> 19:34.549
The ceiling is

19:35.383 --> 19:36.384
so high!

19:40.138 --> 19:42.140
I thought I was falling up.

19:46.269 --> 19:47.771
Thanks for your business!

19:48.271 --> 19:50.607
SALTED MEAT AND POTATO SOUP
YUMMY DELICIOUS SOUP

19:50.690 --> 19:51.941
PLEASURE BAR

19:52.025 --> 19:54.569
Hey, handsome, how about a drink?

19:54.652 --> 19:57.489
You can bring that in with you.

19:59.282 --> 20:01.493
No, thanks. I'm gonna eat at home.

20:05.955 --> 20:08.083
Can I even eat all this by myself?

20:13.672 --> 20:17.384
You've grown so much
since we last saw each other.

20:18.593 --> 20:22.514
You're covered in scars.
It must've been hard.

20:22.597 --> 20:25.517
Robin! What is this? Stop it!

20:25.600 --> 20:29.270
What? I'm just conducting
a small experiment.

20:30.814 --> 20:33.650
Who's inside this head of yours?

20:33.733 --> 20:35.652
I said. It's me!

20:35.735 --> 20:37.487
Say your name.

20:38.613 --> 20:40.031
It's Haruki!

20:41.366 --> 20:42.409
Really?

20:43.827 --> 20:45.829
All right. Take a look in the mirror.

20:52.168 --> 20:54.879
Who's on the bed with me?

20:56.381 --> 20:58.883
Who is that girl?

21:00.093 --> 21:01.845
S-Sis.

21:01.928 --> 21:05.181
Right! It's the sister you love so much.

21:05.682 --> 21:08.351
She's about to be held by another man.

21:08.852 --> 21:10.437
Shouldn't you save her?

21:10.937 --> 21:12.772
Stop it.

21:12.856 --> 21:14.441
Robin, why are you…

21:16.192 --> 21:20.280
Now, whose body am I touching?

21:20.864 --> 21:22.073
Tell me, Haruki.

21:23.116 --> 21:24.868
Robin…

21:24.951 --> 21:26.286
Haruki.

21:26.786 --> 21:28.455
HARUKI TAKEHAYA - GENDER
AGE: 18 - BLOOD TYPE

21:29.664 --> 21:30.832
Robin!

21:35.545 --> 21:36.629
No.

21:37.797 --> 21:40.383
Not me. Look in the mirror, Haruki.

21:41.092 --> 21:44.846
Watch what I'm gonna do to your sister.

22:01.363 --> 22:03.365
It's so blue and dazzling.

22:08.620 --> 22:09.746
<i>It's so pretty.</i>

22:09.829 --> 22:10.830
OUTSIDE OF THE OUTSIDE
